From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/display: keep the 5K iMac DP tile receiver powered

When DC takes over the display from the firmware, it puts every
connected DP receiver into D3. On the iMacPro1,1 the DP tile of the 5K
panel then sometimes does not answer AUX at the next modeset, link
training of the tile fails and the tile shows no image of its own.

Do not put the DP tile receiver of the 5K iMacs into D3.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
  drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_phy.c | 4 ++++
  1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_phy.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_phy.c
index 49521ac..cbf9b59 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_phy.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/dc/link/protocols/link_dp_phy.c
@@ -50,6 +50,10 @@ void dpcd_write_rx_power_ctrl(struct dc_link *link, bool on)
 	if (link->sync_lt_in_progress)
 		return;
 
+	/* The DP tile of the 5K iMacs does not always answer AUX after D3 */
+	if (!on && link->dc->config.imac5K_support && link->link_index == 1)
+		return;
+
 	core_link_write_dpcd(link, DP_SET_POWER, &state,
 						 sizeof(state));
 
